2	 * The conductor — one place that decides what reaches the writer, and when.
3	 *
4	 * It reads the rhythm of the keys (`flow-state.ts`), fits that reading to
5	 * this writer (`flow-profile.ts`), gathers what the room, the Apparatus, the
6	 * shelf, the writer's other work, the charter and the dossier have to offer
7	 * (`flow-items.ts`), and lets through only what the moment allows:
8	 *
9	 *   in flow        the page stands alone; Twyne slips into focus by itself
10	 *   settling       the chrome dims; nothing new arrives
